#question(title: [A counterexample to Alternating Series Test?])[
  Construct a series of the form
  $display(sum_(n = 1)^oo (- 1)^n b_n)$ such
  that
  #set list(spacing: .55em + 0.4cm)
  - $display(b_n > 0)$ for all $n >= 1$
  - $display(lim_(n -> oo) b_n = 0)$
  - the series
    $display(sum_(n = 1)^oo (- 1)^n b_n)$ is
    divergent.
]
